; Mesa's lavapipe as the system's Vulkan driver: what a driver installer
; (or mesa-dist-win's deployment of lavapipe) writes for the Khronos
; loader, vulkan-1.dll, which reads each value's name as the path of an
; ICD manifest (a DWORD 0: enabled). The manifest and vulkan_lvp.dll it
; names are in System32 (PREBUILT mesa). Loaded after registry.seed
; (module string `registry`); ARCHITECTURE "Software 3D (G2)".

[\Registry\Machine\SOFTWARE\Khronos\Vulkan\Drivers]
"C:\Windows\System32\lvp_icd.x86_64.json"=dword:0
